"1847","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no zakat due on less than five camels, and nothing on four. When they reach five, a sheep is due until they reach nine. When they reach ten, two sheep are due until they reach fourteen. When they reach fifteen, three sheep are due until they reach nineteen. When they reach twenty, four sheep are due until they reach twenty-four. When they reach twenty-five, a bint makhad (one-year-old female camel) is due up to thirty-five. If a bint makhad is not available, then an ibn labun (two-year-old male camel). If the number increases by one camel, a bint labun (two-year-old female camel) is due until they reach forty-five. If the number increases by one camel, a hiqqah (three-year-old female camel) is due until they reach sixty. If the number increases by one camel, a jadh'ah (four-year-old female camel) is due until they reach seventy-five. If the number increases by one camel, two bint labun are due until they reach ninety. If the number increases by one camel, two hiqqah are due until they reach one hundred and twenty. Thereafter, for every fifty camels a hiqqah is due, and for every forty camels a bint labun is due."""
